---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import InputGroupDemo from "../../components/InputGroupDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Input Group"
  description="One bordered field made of an input or textarea and its icons, text, shortcuts, and buttons, from search boxes to the chat composer."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Input Group</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    One bordered field made of a control and its additions: icons, prefixes,
    shortcuts, and buttons. It powers search boxes, the workspace URL field,
    combobox inputs, picker searches, and the chat composer.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><InputGroupDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Input Group usage"
      code={`import {
  InputGroup,
  InputGroupAddon,
  InputGroupButton,
  InputGroupInput,
  InputGroupText,
  InputGroupTextarea,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/input-group";

// Search with a clear button
<InputGroup>
  <InputGroupAddon><Search3 size={14} aria-hidden="true" /></InputGroupAddon>
  <InputGroupInput ref={input} aria-label="Search chat titles" placeholder="Search chat titles"
    maxLength={640} value={query} onChange={event => setQuery(event.target.value)} />
  <InputGroupAddon align="inline-end">
    {query && (
      <InputGroupButton size="icon-xs" aria-label="Clear search"
        onClick={() => { setQuery(""); input.current?.focus(); }}>
        <X aria-hidden="true" />
      </InputGroupButton>
    )}
  </InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>

// Large, with a text prefix
<InputGroup size="lg">
  <InputGroupAddon><InputGroupText>app.tulipfarm.ai/</InputGroupText></InputGroupAddon>
  <InputGroupInput id="workspace-slug" required maxLength={48}
    aria-invalid={Boolean(error)} aria-describedby="workspace-slug-hint" />
</InputGroup>

// Composer
<InputGroup variant={questionPending ? "question-composer" : "composer"}>
  <InputGroupAddon align="block-start">{attachments}</InputGroupAddon>
  <InputGroupTextarea aria-label="Message" placeholder="Ask anything…" />
  <InputGroupAddon align="block-end" className="border-t">
    <DropdownMenuTrigger render={<InputGroupButton size="sm" aria-label="Add a file" />}>
      <Paperclip aria-hidden="true" /> Files
    </DropdownMenuTrigger>
    <InputGroupButton type="submit" size="icon-sm"
      variant={canSend ? "default" : "secondary"} aria-label="Send message">
      <ArrowUp aria-hidden="true" />
    </InputGroupButton>
  </InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>

// Base UI Combobox renders through the group parts
<InputGroup>
  <Combobox.Input render={<InputGroupInput />} aria-label="Choose a fruit" />
  <InputGroupAddon align="inline-end">
    <InputGroupButton size="icon-xs" render={<Combobox.Trigger />} aria-label="Show fruits">
      <ChevronDown aria-hidden="true" />
    </InputGroupButton>
    <Combobox.Clear render={<InputGroupButton size="icon-xs" />} aria-label="Clear selection">
      <X aria-hidden="true" />
    </Combobox.Clear>
  </InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>InputGroup</code> takes <code>size</code>: <code>default</code>
      (32px, 14px text) or <code>lg</code> (44px, 16px text), and
      <code>variant</code>: <code>default</code>, <code>composer</code> (a stacked
      message box with a stronger border and panel radius), or
      <code>question-composer</code> (the same box with a quieter border while an
      agent waits on an answer). It is a <code>div</code> with
      <code>role="group"</code> and takes every div prop.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>InputGroupAddon</code> takes <code>align</code>:
      <code>inline-start</code> (default), <code>inline-end</code>,
      <code>block-start</code>, or <code>block-end</code>. It can come before or
      after the control in markup. Block additions turn the group into a column;
      add <code>border-b</code> or <code>border-t</code> for a divider row.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>InputGroupButton</code> is a Sprout <code>Button</code> with
      <code>size</code>
      <code>xs</code> (default), <code>sm</code>,
      <code>icon-xs</code>, or <code>icon-sm</code>, any Button
      <code>variant</code> (default <code>ghost</code>), and
      <code>type="button"</code> unless set. Use <code>render</code> to make it a
      menu, popover, tooltip, or combobox trigger.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>InputGroupInput</code> and <code>InputGroupTextarea</code> are Sprout
      <code>Input</code> and <code>Textarea</code> without their own border and fill.
      They take every native prop and read a surrounding
      <code>Field</code>. <code>InputGroupText</code> is muted text for prefixes,
      units, and shortcuts.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Behavior</h2>
    <p>
      The group draws the border, focus ring, and invalid and disabled states
      for any element marked <code>data-slot="input-group-control"</code>.
      <code>InputGroupInput</code> and <code>InputGroupTextarea</code> set it; add
      it to a rich text editor to get the same states. A control without it, like
      a command list's search input, keeps the group quiet.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clicking an addon anywhere except a button focuses the control, like a
      label. Inside a combobox popup the group skips its focus ring, since the
      list shows where focus is. In the composer, toolbar buttons grow to 44px
      on touch screens.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Name the control with a <code>label</code> or <code>aria-label</code>, and
      name icon-only buttons with <code>aria-label</code>. Icons in addons
      should be <code>aria-hidden</code>. Mark errors with
      <code>aria-invalid</code> and point <code>aria-describedby</code> at the message.
      Keyboard focus shows a 2px ring around the whole group; the composer swaps it
      for a focus-colored border.
    </p>
    <p>
      Border, fill, and ring changes take 120ms and stop when reduced motion is
      requested. In forced colors mode the group keeps a system border and a
      highlight focus ring.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The border uses <code>--sprout-input</code> (composer:
      <code>--sprout-border</code>), the fill <code>--sprout-surface</code>, and
      addon text <code>--sprout-muted</code>. Focus uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>, errors <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and
      disabled <code>--sprout-hover</code>. Radius follows
      <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>, or
      <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code> for composers. The opt-in TulipFarm theme
      tints the focus ring and send button through these tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
